  "doc": {
    "doi": "10.1080/01916122.2022.2150904",
    "citation": "Steemans P, Sariaslan N, Cascales-Miñana B, Langer MR, Meienbrock W, Servais T. 2023. A diverse Early Devonian palynoflora from the Waxweiler Lagerstätte (Klerf Formation, Rhenish Massif, Western Germany): palaeobotanical implications. Palynology 47(2):2150904. [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1080/01916122.2022.2150904).",
    "language": "English",
    "reports_window_spores": true,
    "comment": "The full supplied text and PDF table were examined. Thirteen samples were collected: eleven from Waxweiler and two from Merlscheid. Table 1 contains twelve named sample columns, nine with spore records; WAX2, WAX5 and WAX8 are blank and retained without assuming demonstrated absence. The unnamed second Merlscheid sample was unproductive. Methods inconsistently state that all eleven Waxweiler samples yielded palynomorphs and that nine samples were productive overall. Section 3.1 assigns the shared assemblage to the 'early/middle Emsian'; the abstract instead gives 'earliest Pragian to middle Emsian'. Plate 1 adds four occurrences absent from Table 1: Acinosporites lindlarensis and Verrucosisporites polygonalis in WAX11, and Acinosporites cf. apiculatus and Diatomozonotriletes franklinii in Eifel II-1. Plate slide suffixes WAX11-1 and EIFEL II-1-1 are grouped with their corresponding table samples. Illustration flags are sample-specific. Table spelling 'Retusotriletes triangulates' is retained; the discussion uses 'Retusotriletes cf. triangulatus'. Abundance codes: R, rare (1–2 individuals); C, common (4–10); A, abundant (≥20). Italicised counts denote unusual occurrences. Demonstrated reworking concerns Cambro-Ordovician acritarchs; no spores are identified as reworked."
  },
